+# Source and current-status audit
+
+Checked September 30, 2026. No complete resolution was identified in this bounded primary-source search. Recommended package disposition: unsolved, with no novelty claim.
+
+## Source recovery
+
+The live problem page was unavailable to the web reader. The complete pinned record points to Danny Calegari, *Problems in foliations and laminations of 3-manifolds*, [arXiv:math/0209081v1](https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0209081), September 8, 2002. The arXiv page currently lists one version and a publication reference, Proc. Symp. Pure Math. 71 (2003), 297–335. The accessible primary manuscript is 35 pages.
+
+Question 13.1 is on printed p.29, under Numerical invariants, subsection Godbillon–Vey. That page and all four following remarks were read and visually inspected. The full target is a weak pointwise sign of the Godbillon–Vey density of a fixed minimal taut C² foliation with nonzero invariant on an atoroidal 3-manifold. Its truncated imported title concealed these essential assumptions.
+
+The source's remarks already explain why arbitrary splicing across torus leaves or nonminimal sets would not give a valid counterexample under the hypotheses. Its Euler-class obstruction is explicitly for a strictly contact representative, while the question permits zeros. Question 13.2 asks about tightness under an additional contact assumption; it is not silently merged into Question 13.1.
+
+## Primary literature inspected
+
+- [Hurder–Langevin, Dynamics and the Godbillon–Vey class of C¹ foliations](https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~hurder/papers/59manuscript-rev2016.pdf), manuscript revised August 26, 2016. The introduction and Section3 were read. They distinguish defining forms, nonunique auxiliary forms, the cohomology class, and the dynamical nonvanishing theorem. Nonzero Godbillon–Vey implies a resilient leaf/positive entropy in the stated setting; this does not choose a sign-definite representative.
+- [Calegari's 2012 exposition, Characteristic classes of foliations](https://lamington.wordpress.com/2012/02/21/characteristic-classes-of-foliations/), read as an author exposition. It describes helical wobble and characteristic-class constructions and explicitly is not an up-to-date survey. Its unit-tangent-bundle example is not a counterexample in an atoroidal class.
+- Current searches used the exact question number, monotone-wobble terminology together with Godbillon–Vey, sign-definite/positive representative, and the author's name. Generic newer results on taut foliations, universal circles, and transverse measures did not supply the requested sign theorem. Search-engine noise involving optical-disc wobble was excluded entirely.
+
+The search is not a proof that no resolution exists. The artifact therefore reports that this attempt failed to resolve the exact target, rather than asserting an exhaustive literature theorem.
+
+## Prior attempt and duplicate gates
+
+No earlier local attempt folder, numeric-ID PR, Godbillon descriptive PR, matching remote branch, state entry, or related-target-group entry was found. The queue row was rank76, queued,0/5. The pinned corpus contains other Godbillon–Vey questions (10300044,10300060,10300067) about bounds, laminations and cobordism; these are distinct targets.
+
+## Scope of the obstruction package
+
+All new calculations are explicitly smooth-category statements. They are standard differential-form and transport arguments with no priority claim. The source asks about C² foliations; no smoothing or regularity upgrade is asserted. The local forms and torus flows used in diagnostics are not promoted to global minimal taut atoroidal examples. The exact unresolved issues are the choice of defining-form gauge and weak-sign smooth attainment after that choice.
